# This repository is PUBLIC. Nothing personal may ever reach it.
#
# The application's data — database, cached card images, exports — lives OUTSIDE
# this repo entirely, in $BINDER_DATA_DIR (default ~/Developer/binder-data/).
# The rules below are the second line of defence, not the first.

# --- the collection itself: irreplaceable, personal, never committed ----------
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
binder-data/
/data/

# Cached and normalised card images. Sourced from the web, re-derivable, and
# large. Andy's own card photographs are personal and must never be committed.
/images/
/card-images/
/image-cache/
*.heic
*.HEIC

# --- secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
# There are none yet. When a pricing-API token arrives it is an environment
# variable, never a file in the tree. On a public repo a committed token is a
# live credential leak, not a mistake you can quietly fix in a later commit.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json

# --- build output and dependencies -------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- test and tooling artefacts ----------------------------------------------
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
playwright/.cache/

# --- local tool state ---------------------------------------------------------
# .claude/ holds per-machine permissions, not project config. Project guidance
# lives in CLAUDE.md at the repo root, which IS committed — a clone must carry
# the operating rules with it.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- OS noise -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db

# --- logs ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
